-- statement:
--   This bundle names the scalar expressions in the switcheroo contraction proof. The definitions expose the first split, the left-front term, the mixed tensor term, and the once-commuted term so the four-term comparison can be related to the operator identities and Cauchy-Schwarz bounds.
--
--   Principal definitions:
--   - `switcherooAggregateLeftFrontScalar`: The scalar expectation of the left-front aggregate product after the second square-root self-consistency step.
--   - `switcherooAggregateFirstSplitScalar`: The scalar obtained by splitting the left-front term by polynomial outcome and inserting the indexed submeasurement outcomes.
--   - `switcherooAggregateOnceCommutedScalar`: The scalar after the first commutation step and its square-root error contribution.
--   - `switcherooAggregateMixedScalar`: The mixed tensor scalar after the first self-consistency move in the fourth-term chain.
--
